{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAH61ZPvBvmL1J8NiKk4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've submitted index 1 (Sb fraction 0.195) as the best composition. At 0.039% it had the highest EQE I measured, but I can't tell how close that is to the true best on the line. I used all 5 EQE measurements and 4 of the 5 XRD measurements.\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 0.15 | 0.023 |\n| **1** | **0.195** | **0.039** |\n| 4 | 0.32 | 0.015 |\n| 14 | 0.50 | 0.008 |\n| 22 | 0.66 | 0.010 |\n\n- **Trend:** EQE is best on the Pb-rich side and peaks near Sb 0.2. It drops at Sb 0.15 and stays low from about 0.3 upward. Index 14 is close to the Pb₂Sb₂O₇ ratio, where you might expect the best result, but it measured the lowest EQE of the five.\n- **XRD:** The film's own crystalline phase gives the strongest peaks at low Sb. By Sb 0.5 it has faded and the substrate peaks dominate. Index 1 also shows two weak extra peaks from a small second, lead-rich phase.\n- **Uncertainty:** Indices 2 and 3 (Sb 0.26 and 0.29) weren't measured because I had no EQE budget left. The only thing that brackets the peak on that side is the drop to 0.015% at Sb 0.32, so one of those two could beat index 1.\n\nThe runner-up measurements and the Pb₂Sb₂O₇ idea went in as rejected alternatives, each with its reason."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":676,"cache_read_input_tokens":7893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":676},"output_tokens":550,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c03a4e90-c5cf-4565-a289-02ceaf798f27","uuid":"019e0606-82ee-4b8a-a1b8-da68a76bda28","timestamp":"2026-09-18T04:31:49.283Z","request_id":"req_011CfAH616cWAKMyVghT7JSV"}
